Eliminate per-digit Image allocation in symbol drawing.

drawSymbolNumber, drawSymbolString and drawFixedSizeSymbolString each called
getScaledCopy() once per character per frame, allocating a throwaway Image
each time. Between them these render the score readout, the accuracy
percentage, the combo counter and the combo number on every hit circle, so
they are the largest per-frame allocation source in the gameplay path.

Image.draw(x, y, w, h) renders at an arbitrary size from the same
TextureRegion without allocating.

Behavioural note: the digit images are now shared GameImage instances rather
than per-draw copies, so setAlpha() mutates shared state and persists.
drawSymbolNumber therefore gains a setAlpha(1f) reset that the original did
not need. drawSymbolString and drawFixedSizeSymbolString already reset alpha.

The advance width is now computed as a float (width * scale) instead of
reading getWidth() off a scaled copy, which truncated to int. This makes
glyph advance marginally more precise rather than less.

